menu "agent_link SDK"

config AGENT_LINK_OTA_ENABLE
    bool "Enable OTA firmware upgrade over the App link"
    default y
    help
        Handle 0x37 StartOtaUpgrade / 0x56 AbortOtaUpgrade and stream the new firmware
        in over the L2CAP data channel, then verify SHA-256 and reboot into it.
        the official App upgrades agent_link devices with the code path it already ships.
        Requires an OTA-capable partition table (ota_0/ota_1 + otadata).

if AGENT_LINK_OTA_ENABLE

config AGENT_LINK_OTA_REQUIRE_NEWER_VERSION
    bool "Reject firmware that is not strictly newer"
    default n
    help
        y = rule: the version in 0x37 must be strictly greater
        than the running one (major.minor.patch), otherwise the device answers 2030
        OtaVersionIncompat. Same version or a downgrade is refused.

        n (default) = accept any version. This is what lets a bench device be flashed
        back and forth between agent_link firmware (2.x) and the production 1.7.x image
        without a serial cable. The App still decides what it offers.

config AGENT_LINK_OTA_REQUIRE_MODEL_MATCH
    bool "Reject firmware built for a different device model"
    default y
    help
        The App may append a model string to 0x37. When it does and this is enabled, it
        must equal this device's model (agent_link_config_t.model) or the device answers
        2037 OtaModelMismatch — this is what stops a build for other hardware from being
        flashed onto this one. An App that sends no model is always allowed through
        (older App versions)

config AGENT_LINK_OTA_RX_BUFFER_KB
    int "OTA receive buffer (KB)"
    range 16 128
    default 32
    help
        Ring buffer between the link RX callback and the flash-writing worker. Allocated
        in PSRAM when available, otherwise internal RAM. The link is back-pressured (the
        peer stops getting credit) whenever less than a quarter of it is free, so a
        smaller buffer costs throughput, never correctness.

endif # AGENT_LINK_OTA_ENABLE

endmenu
